      "text": "We can eliminate the middle terms in the arithmetic progression to obtain the equation $2a = 10 + ab$. Simplifying this equation using cross multiplication, we obtain $b = \\frac{10}{2-a}$. \n\nNext, we investigate the function $f(a) = b(\\text{arbitrary value}),$ where $b$ must still be a valid term of the sequence. $b = \\frac{10}{2-a}$ is equal to $2$ if and only if $a = \\frac{3}{2}$. If $a \\not= \\frac{3}{2},$ the function $f(a)$ will be negative, since $ab < 0$ in this case. Therefore, $a = \\frac{3}{2}$ is the $a$ where $10, a, b, ab$ will be an arithmetic progression.\n\nSubmission Form",
